export const PRIVACY_EN = "# soluma Privacy Policy\n\n**Effective Date**: May 22, 2026\n\n---\n\n**ROOT CO., Ltd** (\"Company\") values user privacy and complies with applicable laws including Korea's Personal Information Protection Act (PIPA), the Information and Communications Network Act, the U.S. California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA), and the EU GDPR.\n\nThis Policy applies to the mobile application **\"soluma\"** (\"Service\").\n\n---\n\n## 1. Information We Collect\n\n### 1.1 Required Information\n| Category | Items |\n|----------|-------|\n| Registration (Email) | Email, encrypted password |\n| Social Login | KakaoTalk / Google / Apple account identifier and email |\n| Profile | Nickname or name |\n\n### 1.2 Auto-collected During Service Use\n- Christ Test / Faith Checkup responses and results\n- Bible reading, transcription, devotion, plan activity records\n- Community posts (prayers, testimonies, small groups, challenges)\n- Credit top-up and usage history\n- License Pass and subscription holdings/usage\n- Gift send/receive records\n- Talent earn/use records\n- AI counseling conversation content\n- Push notification token (Firebase Cloud Messaging)\n- Device information (OS version, app version, device model)\n- IP address, login time, usage logs\n\n### 1.3 Optional (with consent)\n- Affiliated church information\n- Ministry registration details\n- Talent registration: skill/expertise info\n- Profile photo\n\n### 1.4 Payment Information\n- The Company does **not** directly collect or store payment details (credit card numbers, etc.).\n- All payments are processed via Apple App Store / Google Play in-app purchases.\n- The Company only receives and stores payment results (product ID, amount, timestamp, receipt).\n\n## 2. Purposes of Collection and Use\n\n| Purpose | Items |\n|---------|-------|\n| Account management | Email, social account, nickname |\n| Personalized Service | Test responses, activity records, profile |\n| Payment and subscription management | Receipt, product ID, holdings |\n| AI analysis/counseling | Test results, pseudonymized input |\n| Community operation | Posts, comments, group memberships |\n| Push notifications | Device token |\n| Customer support | Email, inquiry content |\n| Service quality improvement | Usage logs, device info (pseudonymized) |\n| Anti-fraud and abuse prevention | IP, activity records |\n\n## 3. Retention Period\n\n- Generally **deleted immediately upon membership withdrawal**\n- Retained for legal periods in the following cases:\n\n| Retained Items | Period | Legal Basis |\n|----------------|--------|-------------|\n| Contract or withdrawal records | 5 years | E-Commerce Act |\n| Payment records | 5 years | E-Commerce Act |\n| Consumer complaint records | 3 years | E-Commerce Act |\n| Marketing display records | 6 months | E-Commerce Act |\n| Connection logs/IP | 3 months | Communications Secrecy Act |\n| Abuse records (if applicable) | 1 year | Internal policy |\n\n## 4. Third-Party Disclosure\n\nWe do not disclose personal information to third parties except:\n\n- With user's prior consent\n- When required by law\n- When validly requested by investigative authorities\n\n## 5. Processing Entrustment\n\n| Processor | Purpose | Data Location |\n|-----------|---------|---------------|\n| **Supabase** (Supabase Inc., USA) | Auth, database hosting | USA |\n| **OpenAI** (OpenAI, L.L.C., USA) | AI counseling/analysis (pseudonymized) | USA |\n| **Firebase / Google Cloud** (Google LLC, USA) | Push notifications, cloud infra | USA, etc. |\n| **Apple App Store** (Apple Inc., USA) | iOS in-app payments | USA |\n| **Google Play** (Google LLC, USA) | Android in-app payments | USA, etc. |\n\n**International Transfer**: These processors store data in the USA and elsewhere. Users consent to this transfer upon registration.\n\n## 6. Data Deletion\n\n### Procedure\n- Deleted without delay upon withdrawal or retention period expiry.\n- For legally required retention, data is segregated and deleted at period end.\n\n### Method\n- **Electronic files**: Permanently deleted via irrecoverable means.\n- **Paper documents**: Shredded or incinerated.\n\n## 7. User Rights\n\nUsers may exercise the following rights at any time:\n\n1. **Access** request\n2. **Correction/Deletion** request\n3. **Processing Halt** request\n4. **Consent Withdrawal** and **membership withdrawal**\n\n**Method**: In-app **Settings > Profile** / **Settings > Withdraw**, or email **master@root2christ.com**\n\n## 8. Protection of Children Under 14\n\n1. The Company does not knowingly collect data from children under 14.\n2. Registration under 14 requires **parental consent**.\n3. U.S. children under 13 are protected under COPPA; parental consent is required.\n\n## 9. California (USA) Resident Rights (CCPA)\n\nCalifornia residents have the following rights under CCPA:\n\n1. **Right to Know** — about collected personal info and its use\n2. **Right to Delete**\n3. **Right to Opt-Out of Sale** (※ the Company does not sell personal information)\n4. **Right to Non-Discrimination** for exercising rights\n\nContact: **master@root2christ.com**\n\n## 10. EU/EEA Resident Rights (GDPR)\n\nEU/EEA residents have rights including **data portability**, **right to object to automated decision-making**, in addition to the above.\n\n## 11. Safety Measures\n\n- **Encryption**: One-way password hashing, SSL/TLS for transport\n- **Access Control**: Restricted access to personal data processing systems\n- **Access Log retention and review**\n- **Antivirus software**\n- **Minimum staff handling personal info, with training**\n\n## 12. Push Notifications and Marketing\n\n1. We send service-related notifications (devotion, challenges, community).\n2. Users may toggle notifications in **Settings > Notifications**.\n3. **Advertising-purpose messages** require separate consent.\n\n## 13. Cookies and Analytics\n\nWe may collect pseudonymized usage logs for service improvement. We do not use separate ad-tracking cookies.\n\n## 14. Privacy Officer\n\n| Item | Detail |\n|------|--------|\n| **Officer** | PARK SANG BUM (CEO) |\n| **Organization** | ROOT CO., Ltd |\n| **Email** | master@root2christ.com |\n| **Address** | 65 Yeomdon-ro, Seogwipo-si, Jeju-do, Republic of Korea |\n\n## 15. Grievance Resolution\n\nKorean residents may contact:\n- **Privacy Portal**: privacy.go.kr (182)\n- **Personal Information Dispute Mediation Committee**: kopico.go.kr (1833-6972)\n\nU.S. residents:\n- **California Attorney General's Office** (oag.ca.gov/privacy)\n\n## 16. Policy Changes\n\nThis Policy may be amended due to legal, policy, or security changes. Changes will be notified in-app at least 7 days before the effective date.\n\n---\n\n**Supplementary Provisions**\n\nThis Policy takes effect on May 22, 2026.\n";
